README.md "AgentSandbox" section (and the same SYNOPSIS shape in the provider POD) shows

  spec => { replicas => 1, shutdownPolicy => "Retain" }

IO::K8s::AgentSandbox::V1beta1::Sandbox models spec as an inline struct without a replicas field, so Moo discards the key on construction and to_json emits spec => { shutdownPolicy => "Retain" }. Verified 2026-09-03 on master (1.108). Upstream agent-sandbox v1.0.0 Sandbox has no spec.replicas either, so the example is wrong, not the class.

Two parts: (1) fix the example; (2) decide whether an inline-struct spec should reject unknown keys instead of dropping them silently -- the same fail-closed line the k56/k57 AutoGen fixes drew. Part (2) is being settled in the CRD design grill.
